        "original_id": "1381f955-65fd-56a9-ad4e-2d8a88f001d6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Svalbard, Jan Mayen, Svalbard and Jan Mayen, Norway\n- Systems: ISO 3166-1, ISO 3166-1 numeric, UN M.49\n- Organizations: United Nations Statistics Division\n- Topics: Mammals of Svalbard and Jan Mayen\n\nFacts:\n- ISO 3166-1 defines Svalbard and Jan Mayen as a statistical designation for two parts of Norway under separate jurisdictions: Svalbard and Jan Mayen.\n- Svalbard and Jan Mayen has the ISO 3166-1 codes alpha-2 SJ, alpha-3 SJM, and numeric 744.\n- ISO 3166-1 numeric codes are similar to the three-digit country codes developed and maintained by the United Nations Statistics Division and originate from the UN M.49 standard.\n- Svalbard and Jan Mayen has 17 mammal species.\n- In Svalbard and Jan Mayen, 0 mammal species are critically endangered, 3 are endangered, 3 are vulnerable, and 0 are near-threatened.",
